        "original_id": "d48cfb81-e5c8-5c72-830a-ed8fbfbf2045",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Chamelaucium, Vanilla\n- Plant Families and Genera: Myrtaceae, Leptospermum, Orchidaceae\n- Places: south western Western Australia, Mexico\n- Topics: endemic distribution, flavoring sources\n\nFacts:\n- Chamelaucium is a genus of shrubs endemic to south western Western Australia.\n- Chamelaucium is also known as waxflower.\n- Chamelaucium belongs to the myrtle family Myrtaceae.\n- Chamelaucium has flowers similar to those of the tea-trees genus Leptospermum.\n- Vanilla is a flavoring derived from orchids of the genus Vanilla.\n- Vanilla is derived primarily from the Mexican species flat-leaved vanilla, V. planifolia.",
